<title>UK: Russia's Black Sea Novorossiisk oil port shut again.</title>
<headline>Russia's Black Sea Novorossiisk oil port shut again.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea oil export terminal at Novorossiisk, Russia's main crude outlet to European markets, was shut on Friday due to bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port closed at 2230 local time on Thursday, only six hours after reopening following a 10-hour shutdown.</p>
<p>During the interlude, one large tanker completed loading Russian Urals crude oil and another was allowed to berth, the source said.</p>
<p>Berthing operations were also suspended on Friday at the Black Sea port of Tuapse due to high winds and swell, but Odessa was open.</p>
<p>The Baltic port of Ventspils was operating normally, the source said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
